# DVWA Practice — Vulnerability Findings

## Environment
- Target: DVWA (Damn Vulnerable Web Application)
- Security Level: Low
- Date: June 2026

## Finding 1 — SQL Injection
- Payload: 1' UNION SELECT user, password FROM users --+
- Impact: Full database dump — all usernames and password hashes
- OWASP: A05:2025 Injection
- Fix: Parameterized queries

## Finding 2 — Reflected XSS
- Payload: <script>alert(document.cookie)</script>
- Impact: Session cookie exposed — account takeover possible
- OWASP: A05:2025 Injection
- Fix: HTML output encoding

## Finding 3 — Stored XSS
- Payload: <script>alert('Stored XSS')</script>
- Impact: Persistent — fires for every visitor including admins
- OWASP: A05:2025 Injection
- Fix: Input validation + output encoding

## MD5 Hash Cracking
- Hashes cracked instantly using crackstation.net
- Proves MD5 is unsuitable for password storage
- Fix: Use bcrypt or Argon2
